<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.thepoolboy.corestart-reach</id>
  <name>Corestart Reach</name>
  <summary>Manage RDP and SSH connections</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-only</project_license>

  <developer id="io.github.thepoolboy">
    <name>ThePoolboy</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Corestart Reach keeps your remote desktop (RDP) and SSH connections, and the logins
      for them, in one encrypted vault, and opens any of them with a double-click. It's a
      simple, modern connection manager in the spirit of mRemoteNG and Royal TS.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Everything is encrypted with your master password (Argon2id and XChaCha20-Poly1305)</li>
      <li>RDP opens logged in, with clipboard and sound; FreeRDP is included</li>
      <li>SSH opens in its own terminal, with passwords, key files, ssh-agent or 2FA prompts</li>
      <li>Saved credentials shared by many connections, so a password changes in one place</li>
      <li>Quick connect to any host without saving it</li>
      <li>Folders with drag and drop, search and keyboard shortcuts</li>
      <li>Locks itself when you're away</li>
      <li>Light and dark themes</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Free and open source, with no paid version.</p>
  </description>

